{"id": "holcim-2026-09-11-014", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["holcim"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["涉及產能"]}, "title": "Waste to be sent to cement plants in Croatia", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/news/RDF-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>Croatia: </strong>Non-hazardous waste will be sent to cement plants belonging to Holcim Hrvatska and Nexe at a cost of €357,500, according to Prime Minister Andrej Plenković. The waste is being stored at the PPK Velebit site in Gospić. It consists of plastic, tyres and other waste, which will be used in by the cement producers as alternative fuel. The work is deemed ‘urgent’ and will be completed within 45 days.", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21229-waste-to-be-sent-to-cement-plants-in-croatia", "type": "rss"}]}
